CHAPTER V

RIGHTS OF VICTIMS

Article 16

1. Every Victim has the right to: a. the right to have their dignity respected as a human being;
b. the right to health and psychological recovery;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality of their identity;
f. the right to compensation from the perpetrator;
g. the right to Social Rehabilitation;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and/or j. the right to assistance.
2. In addition to the rights as referred to in paragraph (1), Child Victims of Violence have the right to: a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and/or e. the right to obtain freedom.

