b. safe;
c. empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easily accessible; and f. guaranteed confidentiality.

Article 6

1. Prevention of violence against women as referred to in Article 5 letter a is carried out in an integrated manner coordinated by the Regional Apparatus responsible for women's empowerment and child protection.
2. Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by involving: a. families;
b. communities;
c. private sector;
d. community institutions;
e. social institutions; and f. educational institutions.

Article 7

Prevention of violence against women as referred to in Article 6 is implemented among others by: a. forming a network in efforts to prevent violence against women;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns with communities, the private sector and non-governmental organizations; and c. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the protection of women.

Article 3

Protection of women and children victims of violence is implemented based on the principles of:

a. gender responsive;
b. non-discrimination;
c. equal and respectful relationships;
d. maintaining privacy and confidentiality;
e. providing a sense of security and comfort;
f. respecting individual differences;
g. non-judgmental;
h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;
i. sensitive to the background and condition of victims;
j. use of language that is appropriate and understood by victims;
k. fast and simple;
l. empathy; and
m. the best interests of victims.

Article 10

